  "body": "This draft implements the OPICA follow-up to merged PR #293 while preserving all 100 original primary roots and 28 acceptance units. Both foundational PDFs, frozen normative specifications and complete acceptance scope remain required. RH, Step 4 and independent closing inequalities remain OPEN.\n\nCurrent published checkpoint: `6c44ff564df025770a315f9dbfc091fc10ff6f36`\nTree: `acf035882020db4f151bfd4cdd588b22dd276d35`\n\nStage 1 repaired four original candidates: Laguerre tail norm, actual dilated comb Fourier identity, first-cell sign and quantitative negative-mass cost. It added tested full100 receipt production/reading/cold-replay infrastructure, retaining the explicit historical41 subset. The independent full semantic seal remains unset; actual full100 production/replay and release companions remain unfinished and fail closed.\n\nStage 2 implements five original roots with exact-source module saves, imported independent full-type/domain theorem consumers and standard-only transitive axiom closures:\n- native_auxiliary_top_moment\n- native_auxiliary_tail_residual_lower\n- native_terminal_memory_lower\n- weighted_mixture_exists_fourier\n- near_gap_mass_bound\n\nThe native chain uses the actual log-weighted arithmetic drive, actual finite-history residual and required weighted L1 memory. Weighted mixing constructs the noncompact locally finite complex measure with true variation, absolute Fubini, Fourier reflection and exact origin atom. The near-gap mass estimate uses the actual signed Jordan carrier and exact constant; its nonzero dilation-family witness and other three near-gap roots remain OPEN.\n\nCurrent ledger: 41 historical source-bound subset roots; 15 additional narrow local results; 1 unaccepted supplied word/jet candidate; 43 roots without complete implementations. This is not aggregate acceptance of56 roots or a completed release. No supporting lemma is counted as a primary.\n\nValidation:\n- New individual module saves and imported consumers pass warning-free with only propext, Classical.choice and Quot.sound.\n- Child infrastructure suite:185 normal and185 optimized tests pass.\n- Stage1 parent full suite:201 normal and201 optimized pass in genuine Linux, historical scope.\n- Stage2 focused parent documentation:14 tests per mode, ProtectedHistory3 tests, and4 child pin/forgery controls per mode pass.\n- Final689-artifact inventory preparation passes normal and optimized. An earlier stale-inventory preparation failure is retained with its explanation and is not relabelled.\n- Renderer, navigation, frozen100 contract objects, exact source hashes, historical bytes and reviewed staged bytes checked.\n\nBounded all-job harvests and complete Post-Green Research Passes are included. Stage1-head workflows were still queued/pending at the last bounded harvest; no new exact-head whole-package CI or full acceptance is claimed. The supplied word/jet consumer remains unaccepted while genuine inherited dependencies are built.\n\nStart with:\n- [Stage2 handover](https://github.com/HMarcusWH/zeta-23-lean/blob/6c44ff564df025770a315f9dbfc091fc10ff6f36/research/RHRC/integration/opica_followup/continuation/2026-10-22/STAGE2_HANDOVER.md)\n- [100-root ledger](https://github.com/HMarcusWH/zeta-23-lean/blob/6c44ff564df025770a315f9dbfc091fc10ff6f36/research/RHRC/integration/opica_followup/continuation/2026-10-22/ROOT_LEDGER_100.json)\n- [Remaining work](https://github.com/HMarcusWH/zeta-23-lean/blob/6c44ff564df025770a315f9dbfc091fc10ff6f36/research/RHRC/integration/opica_followup/continuation/2026-10-22/REMAINING_WORK.md)\n- [Next-agent task](https://github.com/HMarcusWH/zeta-23-lean/blob/6c44ff564df025770a315f9dbfc091fc10ff6f36/research/RHRC/integration/opica_followup/continuation/2026-10-22/NEXT_AGENT_PROMPT.md)\n\nFull expected-type/domain coverage, all missing roots/canonical definitions, facade and registration, compiler-derived dependencies, parent/runtime/canonical/workflow release companions and final exact-head research harvest remain mandatory.",
